# Phased Implementation Plan: Personal Site + Portfolio on Astro + Svelte 5

*Research report for Claude Code / Superpowers spec-driven workflow. April 2026.*

---

## 0. Executive Answers to the Critical Questions

Before the phased plan, here are the verified, falsifiable answers to the 20 research questions. Everything below the line is grounded in these facts.

- **Astro version.** The current stable line is **Astro 6.0**, released 10 March 2026, introducing a built-in Fonts API, stable Content Security Policy API, stable Live Content Collections, a Vite 7–powered dev server that runs the same runtime as production (including `workerd` for Cloudflare), and Zod 4 ([Astro 6.0 release notes](https://astro.build/blog/astro-6/)). Node 22.12+ is now required ([svelte integration changelog](https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/integrations/svelte/CHANGELOG.md)). **Use Astro 6.x.**
- **Content Layer vs legacy collections.** Astro 5 replaced the legacy `type: 'content'` system with the **Content Layer API** (`src/content.config.ts`, `loader: glob()` / `file()` / custom), delivering ~5× faster Markdown and ~2× faster MDX builds with 25–50 % less memory; Astro 6 made Live Content Collections stable on top of that API ([Astro Content Collections docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/content-collections/), [Astro 6.0](https://astro.build/blog/astro-6/)). Legacy collections are removed in v6 ([Southwell Media – Astro 6 upgrade notes](https://www.southwellmedia.com/blog/astro-6-whats-coming-2026)). **Use Content Layer with `glob()` loader.**
- **Svelte 5 + Astro.** `@astrojs/svelte` v7+ supports **Svelte 5 with runes** (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`, `$props`). Svelte 5 shipped stable October 2024 and is now the default ([@astrojs/svelte docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/integrations-guide/svelte/), [PkgPulse: Svelte 5 runes](https://www.pkgpulse.com/blog/svelte-5-runes-complete-guide-2026)). Fixes for type checking and `$props.id()` uniqueness across multiple islands are in recent releases ([svelte integration changelog](https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/integrations/svelte/CHANGELOG.md)).
- **Cloudflare.** Cloudflare acquired the Astro company on 16 January 2026; Astro 6's dev server now runs `workerd` locally ([alexbobes – Astro 2026](https://alexbobes.com/programming/a-deep-dive-into-astro-build/)). **Important deprecation:** the `@astrojs/cloudflare` adapter **no longer supports Cloudflare Pages** and now targets **Cloudflare Workers** (with Assets) exclusively ([@astrojs/cloudflare docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/integrations-guide/cloudflare/), [Astro Cloudflare deploy guide](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/deploy/cloudflare/)). Workers Free tier: 100 k requests/day, 10 ms CPU on free / 30 s on paid, unlimited bandwidth ([Cloudflare Workers limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/), [DEV – Cloudflare vs Vercel 2026](https://dev.to/dataformathub/cloudflare-vs-vercel-vs-netlify-the-truth-about-edge-performance-2026-50h0)).
- **Superpowers workflow.** Open-source plugin by Jesse Vincent (`obra/superpowers`) enforcing **brainstorm → spec → plan → subagent execute with TDD + two-stage review → finishing**. Plans break into 2–5-minute tasks; critical review findings block progress ([Builder.io – Superpowers](https://www.builder.io/blog/claude-code-superpowers-plugin), [fsck.com – Superpowers](https://blog.fsck.com/2025/10/09/superpowers/), [ClaudePluginHub listing](https://www.claudepluginhub.com/plugins/obra-superpowers-2)). A related "Superpowers SDD" variant explicitly adds spec-driven development with drift detection ([MCP Market – Superpowers SDD](https://mcpmarket.com/tools/skills/superpowers-sdd-workflow)).

