## 1. Framework Decisions (with evidence)

| Decision | Choice | Falsifiable claim |
|---|---|---|
| Meta-framework | **Astro 6.x** | Astro 6 is the current stable release (10 Mar 2026) and is corporately backed by Cloudflare since Jan 2026 ([Astro 6.0](https://astro.build/blog/astro-6/)). |
| Island framework | **Svelte 5 (runes)** via `@astrojs/svelte` ≥ v7 | Svelte 5 compiles to smaller JS than React/Vue and has 91 % retention in State of JS 2025 ([PkgPulse – Astro vs SvelteKit](https://www.pkgpulse.com/blog/astro-vs-sveltekit-2026), [Programming Helper – Svelte 2026](https://www.programming-helper.com/tech/svelte-2026-91-retention-runes-dx-leader-python)). |
| Games / interactive articles | **Svelte island inside Astro**, not a separate SvelteKit sub-app | The site is content-dominant; SvelteKit is justified "when interactivity dominates every screen" ([xergioalex – Astro + Svelte](https://xergioalex.com/blog/astro-and-svelte-the-future-of-web-development/)). Spin up a separate SvelteKit app only if one game grows into a full SaaS-style experience. |
| Host | **Cloudflare Workers (with Assets)**, not Pages | The official Astro adapter dropped Pages support; Workers is the recommended path for new Astro projects ([@astrojs/cloudflare docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/integrations-guide/cloudflare/)). |
| Rendering | Static-first (`output: 'static'`), SSR only for `/stats` API endpoints | Most of this site doesn't need SSR; sticking to SSG avoids miniflare limitations and keeps free-tier consumption negligible ([Zenn – Astro 6 + Cloudflare case study](https://zenn.dev/miyabitti/articles/92a3e2e94356c1?locale=en)). |
| Package manager | **pnpm** | Fast install, strict node_modules, first-class support from Astro starters and Cloudflare's C3. |
| Linter/formatter | **Biome** (single tool, Rust speed) with **Prettier** only for `.astro`/`.svelte` that Biome doesn't format | Biome replaces ESLint+Prettier for JS/TS; but `.astro` and `.svelte` still need their own plugins. |
| TypeScript | `strict: true`, plus Astro's `strictest` preset (`extends: "astro/tsconfigs/strictest"`). |

