# Phase 0 — Foundations

**Goal:** A deployable, typed, tested Astro 6 skeleton with the design system wired up, on Cloudflare Workers.

**Exit criteria:**
1. `pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm e2e` all pass.
2. `git push` deploys a live `*.workers.dev` page showing a single styled landing page using all three typefaces.
3. Lighthouse score ≥ 95 on mobile for the empty landing page.
4. Design tokens are CSS custom properties exported from one file; Biome + Prettier run clean.

### Batch 0.1 — Repo, tooling, Astro 6 scaffold

**Build:** Git repo, `pnpm init`, Astro 6 project via `npm create cloudflare@latest -- my-site --framework=astro` ([Cloudflare Workers Astro guide](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/framework-guides/web-apps/astro/)), then convert to pnpm workspace. Configure Biome + Prettier + `astro check` + strict TS.

**Libraries / versions (verify via linked sources):**
- `astro` ^6.0 ([astro.build/blog/astro-6](https://astro.build/blog/astro-6/))
- `@astrojs/cloudflare` latest ([docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/integrations-guide/cloudflare/))
- `wrangler` latest (installed by C3)
- `@biomejs/biome` latest — replaces ESLint + Prettier for JS/TS
- `prettier` + `prettier-plugin-astro` + `prettier-plugin-svelte` — for what Biome can't format yet
- Node 22.12+ (required by Astro 6; Node 20 EOL April 2026 — [Southwell Media](https://www.southwellmedia.com/blog/astro-6-whats-coming-2026))

**Spec should contain:** project name, output mode (`static` initially), adapter (`@astrojs/cloudflare`), TypeScript config (`extends "astro/tsconfigs/strictest"`), Biome config with 100-char line length + double quotes + tab indent (or project preference), git hooks via `lefthook`.

**Acceptance tests:**
- `pnpm build` succeeds; `dist/` contains `index.html`.
- `pnpm biome check .` reports zero errors.
- `pnpm astro check` reports zero errors.
- CI (GitHub Actions) runs the above three commands on PR.

