### Batch 0.4 — Design tokens + fonts pipeline

**Build:** CSS custom properties in `src/styles/tokens.css` (colors, spacing scale, type scale, radii, shadows, motion durations). Configure Astro 6 Fonts API for Fraunces and Geist. Self-host Berkeley Mono via `@font-face` in `public/fonts/`.

**Astro 6 Fonts API ([docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/font-provider-reference/)):** declare fonts in `astro.config.mjs`; Astro downloads, caches, generates fallback metrics using `capsize`, and emits preload links automatically ([Astro 6.0 announcement](https://astro.build/blog/astro-6/)). Providers built in: `google`, `fontsource`, `bunny`, plus local files.

**Concrete config:**
```ts
// astro.config.mjs
fonts: [
  { provider: fontProviders.fontsource(),
    name: "Fraunces", cssVariable: "--font-serif",
    weights: ["400 900"], // variable
    optical_sizing: "auto", subsets: ["latin"] },
  { provider: fontProviders.fontsource(),
    name: "Geist", cssVariable: "--font-sans",
    weights: ["100 900"], subsets: ["latin"] },
  { provider: fontProviders.local(),
    name: "Berkeley Mono", cssVariable: "--font-mono",
    variants: [{ src: ["./src/assets/fonts/berkeley-mono.woff2"],
                 weight: 400, style: "normal" }] },
]
```

Fraunces variable axes: opsz, wght, SOFT, WONK ([Self-Hosting Variable Fonts in Astro](https://mattbatman.com/self-hosting-variable-fonts-in-astro/)). Use axes via CSS `font-variation-settings`.

**Berkeley Mono — commercial licensing. Do NOT commit the font files to a public repo.** Berkeley Mono v2 sells a Developer license (~$75 one-time for v1; v2 is now modularized — Web use, Print, etc., each billed separately) ([Berkeley Graphics product page](https://berkeleygraphics.com/typefaces/berkeley-mono/), [HN thread on Berkeley Mono licensing](https://brianlovin.com/hn/30557557)). Options:
  1. Purchase the web license, store the `.woff2` in the repo but **gitignore it in a public mirror**, or keep the repo private.
  2. Ship self-hosted from a private Cloudflare R2 bucket with a Referer-restricted binding.
  3. **Fallback (recommended to ship first, swap later):** use **Commit Mono** (SIL OFL, free commercial use, [commitmono.com](https://commitmono.com/)), **JetBrains Mono** (OFL, closest free match to Berkeley at ~85 % similarity per [FontAlternatives](https://fontalternatives.com/alternatives/berkeley-mono/)), or **Ioskeley Mono** — an Iosevka build specifically tuned to mimic Berkeley Mono ([ahatem/IoskeleyMono](https://github.com/ahatem/IoskeleyMono)). This lets the site ship on Phase 0 without waiting on a license purchase.

**Grain overlay (token batch, because it's a visual foundation):**
- **Recommended: pre-rendered PNG/WebP noise** on a fixed-position full-viewport layer with `mix-blend-mode: overlay; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.04`. Reason: inline `<feTurbulence>` SVG re-renders every paint and burns CPU on low-end devices; a 256×256 PNG tiled costs ~3 KB gzipped and is cached forever.
- Alternative: SVG turbulence rendered once to an offscreen canvas → `toDataURL("image/png")` at build time. Ship the PNG. (Falsifiable: measure paint time in Chrome DevTools; PNG overlay should add <1 ms per frame vs 3–8 ms for live feTurbulence on a mid-tier laptop.)

**Layout primitives:** `<Stack>`, `<Cluster>`, `<Grid>`, `<Frame>` as `.astro` components using CSS Grid / Flex with tokens. Hairline borders = `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent)` so they adapt to any bg.

**Acceptance tests:**
- Visual regression snapshot (Playwright) of the typography specimen page showing all three families.
- `document.fonts.ready` resolves within 200 ms on preview build.
- No FOIT (font-display: swap active by default in Astro Fonts API).
- `curl /fonts/…woff2` returns `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`.

