# Phase 1 — Card Grid MVP

**Goal:** Home page renders a grid of heterogeneous cards (code / video / music / math / writing) sourced from MDX files, with per-type thumbnail shapes and uniform outer shell. No interactivity yet.

**Exit criteria:** Adding a new `.mdx` file with correct frontmatter causes a new card to appear on the homepage; build fails on schema violation.

### Batch 1.1 — Content schema: one collection, discriminated union

**Build:** A single collection `works` (or `items`) using `z.discriminatedUnion("type", [...])` over the five types. **Recommendation: one collection, not five.** Reasoning:
- The homepage is one heterogeneous grid; keeping items in one collection means `getCollection("works")` returns a sortable list without manual merging.
- Discriminated unions give per-type TypeScript narrowing ([Astro content collections guide](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/content-collections/)).
- Per-type detail pages can still filter by `data.type === "video"`.

Counter-argument: five collections give stricter per-directory file layout and decouple schemas. But that costs ergonomics at the grid level. Prefer one collection; if schemas diverge wildly later, refactor.

**Libraries / versions:**
- `zod` — **Astro 6 ships Zod 4 internally; import from `astro/zod`** to guarantee version alignment ([Southwell Media](https://www.southwellmedia.com/blog/astro-6-whats-coming-2026)).
- `@astrojs/mdx` — current major matching Astro 6.

**Example schema:**
```ts
// src/content.config.ts
import { z, defineCollection } from "astro/zod";
import { glob } from "astro/loaders";

const base = {
  title: z.string(),
  slug: z.string().optional(),
  date: z.coerce.date(),
  updated: z.coerce.date().optional(),
  tags: z.array(z.string()).default([]),
  draft: z.boolean().default(false),
  summary: z.string().max(240).optional(),
  cover: z.object({ src: z.string(), alt: z.string() }).optional(),
};

const works = defineCollection({
  loader: glob({ pattern: "**/*.{md,mdx}", base: "./src/content/works" }),
  schema: z.discriminatedUnion("type", [
    z.object({ type: z.literal("code"),    ...base,
               repo: z.string().url().optional(), stack: z.array(z.string()) }),
    z.object({ type: z.literal("video"),   ...base,
               duration: z.number(), youtube: z.string().optional() }),
    z.object({ type: z.literal("music"),   ...base,
               bpm: z.number().optional(), listen: z.string().url().optional() }),
    z.object({ type: z.literal("math"),    ...base,
               pdf: z.string().optional(), arxiv: z.string().optional() }),
    z.object({ type: z.literal("writing"), ...base,
               wordCount: z.number().optional(), readingTime: z.number().optional() }),
  ]),
});

export const collections = { works };
```

**Spec should contain:** the five type variants, required vs optional fields per variant, slug derivation rule (filename stem if not overridden), draft handling (hidden in production only).

**Acceptance tests:**
- Seed 10 fixture `.mdx` files (two per type); `getCollection("works")` returns 10 items with correctly narrowed types.
- Invalid frontmatter fails `astro check` with a Zod error pointing to the line.
- Draft filtering: `import.meta.env.PROD` hides `draft: true`.

