# Phase 2 — Interactivity

**Goal:** The grid supports URL-synced filters/sort, local search, and keyboard/cmd-K navigation. All powered by Svelte 5 islands, hydrating only what's necessary.

**Exit criteria:** User can `?type=video&tag=synth&sort=title` and get the correct filtered grid on both first paint (SSG prerendered) and subsequent client interactions; cmd-K opens a search palette.

### Batch 2.1 — URL-synced filter + sort state

**Build:** A `<FilterBar client:load>` Svelte 5 island that reads `URLSearchParams` on mount via `$state` + `$derived`, writes back via `history.replaceState`, and dispatches an event consumed by `<Grid client:visible>`.

**Library choice:** `nuqs` is **React-only** (as of April 2026); it has no Svelte port. **Recommendation: roll your own tiny helper.** ~30 lines of TS wrapping `URLSearchParams` + `history.replaceState` + a Svelte `$state` rune. Avoid `svelte-url` and similar abandoned packages.

**Server-side parity:** For SEO and no-JS users, the Astro page reads `Astro.url.searchParams` during prerender if the filter is in the URL at request time (requires SSR pages or pre-generating common filter URLs via `getStaticPaths`). For pure SSG, the filter bar is a progressive enhancement that only works with JS. Document this as a known limitation in the spec.

**Spec:** filter keys (`type`, `tag`, `sort`), allowed values, URL canonicalization (omit defaults), debounce (none — it's synchronous DOM filter).

**Acceptance tests:**
- E2E: click a type chip → URL updates without a navigation → grid updates → back button restores prior state.
- With JS disabled (Playwright `javaScriptEnabled: false`), the full grid still renders (progressive enhancement).

---

### Batch 2.2 — Local search via Pagefind

**Build:** Install `astro-pagefind` integration; add `<Search />` component on `/search` and a small hook in cmd-K.

**Libraries:**
- `astro-pagefind` ([shishkin/astro-pagefind](https://github.com/shishkin/astro-pagefind)) — wraps Pagefind v1.x as an Astro integration that runs after build against `dist/` and uses the last built index during dev ([scottwillsey.com](https://scottwillsey.com/astro-pagefind/)).
- `pagefind` ^1.x — the underlying Rust-built static search tool ([pagefind.app](https://pagefind.app/)).

**Why Pagefind over Fuse.js / MiniSearch:**
- Pagefind is purpose-built for static sites; it lazily loads chunked index segments so the browser downloads <100 KB for a first search on a site of hundreds of pages ([pagefind.app](https://pagefind.app/)).
- Fuse.js requires shipping the full searchable corpus as JSON; on ~500 pages that's multi-megabyte.
- Pagefind is Starlight's default ([Starlight site search](https://starlight.astro.build/guides/site-search/)) — battle-tested in 2026 on doc sites with thousands of pages.
- MiniSearch is faster than Fuse.js but still requires shipping the full corpus.

**Spec:** what gets indexed (`<main>` only; exclude nav / footer with `data-pagefind-ignore`), what gets surfaced as metadata for per-type ranking, URL of search page, cmd-K integration hook.

**Acceptance tests:**
- Searching "synthesizer" on a fixture of 50 items returns the two music posts with that term.
- Bundle size: first-load JS for `/search` < 100 KB (measured in Playwright with `page.route`).
- Search works on built preview only — document the "no search in dev" gotcha in the spec.

