### Batch 2.3 — Cmd-K palette (Svelte 5 island)

**Build:** A Svelte 5 component triggered by ⌘K/Ctrl-K, rendering an overlay with fuzzy-matched list of: pages, recent writings, top tags, and Pagefind search results for typed queries. Use `cmdk-sv` for the base primitive.

**Library options (evaluated April 2026):**

| Option | Pros | Cons | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| `cmdk-sv` ([cmdk-sv.com](https://www.cmdk-sv.com/), port of Paco Coursey's cmdk) | Closest API to the React original, unstyled primitives, accessible | Active maintenance status varies; check commits in repo before committing | **Primary choice** |
| `svelte-command-palette` ([docs](https://svelte-command-palette.vercel.app/), [repo](https://github.com/rohitpotato/svelte-command-palette)) | Svelte 5 ready, Fuse.js fuzzy search built in, ~5 KB gzipped, action-based API | Higher-level / more opinionated | **Backup choice** if cmdk-sv lags |
| `@mateothegreat/svelte5-command-palette` ([repo](https://github.com/mateothegreat/svelte5-command-palette)) | Explicitly Svelte 5 | Less proven | Fallback |
| `kbar` (React) inside `client:only="react"` | Proven | Adds React runtime to a Svelte-primary site for one component | Rejected — framework bloat |
| Roll your own | Full control | ~200 LOC + accessibility work | Do this if all libs ship fewer than 2 Svelte-5 commits/quarter |

**Spec:** key bindings (⌘K / Ctrl-K to open, ⌘Enter to open in new tab, ↑↓ to nav, Esc to close), actions (Go to…, Search "…", Toggle theme, Copy URL, Share), hydration strategy (`client:idle` — not critical to load with the page).

**Acceptance tests:**
- ⌘K opens palette within 50 ms of first-load readiness.
- Fuzzy match: typing "abot" highlights "About".
- Trap focus inside palette; Esc returns focus to trigger.
- Screen reader announces "Command menu open" (aria-live).

