# Phase 6 — IndieWeb Polish

**Goal:** The site is a first-class IndieWeb citizen: full-text RSS/JSON Feed, webmentions displayed, h-card/h-entry microformats, sitemap, custom 404.

### Batch 6.1 — RSS + JSON Feed

**Build:** `@astrojs/rss` for RSS 2.0 with full-content `<content:encoded>`; a second endpoint for JSON Feed 1.1 (hand-built JSON route).

**Libraries:**
- `@astrojs/rss` latest — ships helpers for full-content including MDX rendering via the `rssSchema` + `renderContent` utilities.

**Spec:** which collections get fed, item fields, full vs summary (full), categories from tags.

**Acceptance tests:** feeds validate against the W3C Feed Validator; full post body appears in `<content:encoded>`.

---

### Batch 6.2 — Sitemap + microformats

**Build:** `@astrojs/sitemap` integration; hand-coded h-card in site footer; h-entry wrapping on each post.

**Libraries:** `@astrojs/sitemap` — current major.

**Spec:** sitemap exclusions (drafts, test pages), h-card fields (name, photo, url, note), h-entry fields (p-name, p-summary, e-content, dt-published, u-url, p-author referencing h-card).

**Acceptance tests:** `indiewebify.me` validator passes; sitemap.xml contains all non-draft routes.

---

### Batch 6.3 — Webmentions (receive + display)

**Build:**
1. Sign up at [webmention.io](https://webmention.io) with the site URL; add `<link rel="webmention" href="https://webmention.io/yoursite.com/webmention" />` to `<head>`.
2. At build time, fetch `https://webmention.io/api/mentions.jf2?target=https://yoursite.com/…` for each page into a JSON cache under `src/data/mentions/`.
3. Render mentions on each post page.
4. Optional POSSE: use [Bridgy Fed](https://fed.brid.gy/docs) to federate posts to Mastodon/Bluesky and receive replies back as webmentions.

**Library options:**
- **Manual fetch at build time** — recommended. Simple script that runs before `astro build`; caches to disk so builds work offline.
- `astro-webmentions` community integration — verify active maintenance; fall back to manual if stale.

**Webmention.io is still operational in 2026** ([IndieWeb Webmention page](https://indieweb.org/Webmention)); Bridgy (classic) for POSSE and Bridgy Fed for federation are both maintained by Ryan Barrett ([Bridgy About](https://brid.gy/about), [Bridgy Fed docs](https://fed.brid.gy/docs)).

**Alternative: giscus** (GitHub Discussions as comments) if the user wants threaded comments and doesn't need IndieWeb interop. Ship both: giscus for long-form discussion, webmentions for IndieWeb interop.

**Spec:** which mention types to display (replies, likes, reposts), moderation (blocklist in frontmatter), where to render (below post), whether to cache JSON in git (yes, for reproducible builds).

**Acceptance tests:** a test target URL shows a seeded fixture mention; build works offline from cache.

