## 3. Superpowers Workflow Templates (proposed, verified against plugin docs)

Superpowers enforces `brainstorm → spec → plan → execute (subagent-driven, TDD) → review → finish` ([Builder.io](https://www.builder.io/blog/claude-code-superpowers-plugin), [ClaudePluginHub](https://www.claudepluginhub.com/plugins/obra-superpowers-2)). Each **batch above** maps to one "plan" with a spec.

### `spec.md` template (per batch)

```markdown
# Spec: <batch name>
## Goal
One-paragraph description of the user-visible outcome.
## Context / invariants
- The site is Astro 6.x on Cloudflare Workers, Svelte 5 islands.
- Output is `static` by default; SSR only where explicitly noted.
- Zero third-party network calls at runtime unless listed.
## Non-goals
Explicitly out of scope for this batch.
## Interfaces
- File paths touched.
- Component props / event shapes.
- URL routes added or changed.
## Success criteria (falsifiable)
- [ ] Command X produces output Y.
- [ ] Lighthouse score ≥ N on route Z.
- [ ] Axe-core passes on route Z.
- [ ] Fixture test F is green.
## Dependencies
Previous batch(es) that must be complete.
## Open questions
Items to resolve during brainstorm phase.
```

### `plan.md` template (per batch)

```markdown
# Plan: <batch name>
## Task list (2–5 min each)
1. Create file `src/…/X.astro` with stub and failing test.
2. Implement behavior B; make test green.
3. Add Playwright e2e for flow F.
4. Update `README.md` with new env var.
## Acceptance tests (RED → GREEN)
- test 1 (path)
- test 2 (path)
## Rollback plan
Commit per task; branch merges as single PR.
## Review checklist
- [ ] Biome clean
- [ ] `astro check` clean
- [ ] No new runtime deps > 10 KB gz without justification
- [ ] Axe-core clean
- [ ] Bundle-size delta < N KB (report it)
```

Superpowers' test-driven-development skill will delete code that precedes a failing test, so every task in the plan must start with a test stub ([ClaudePluginHub](https://www.claudepluginhub.com/plugins/obra-superpowers-2)). Install via: `/plugin install superpowers@claude-plugins-official` ([obra/superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers)).

