## 4. Known Risks & Deprecation Watch

| Item | Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| `@astrojs/cloudflare` dropped Pages support | Already happened; existing Pages docs on third-party blogs are stale | Use Workers with Assets, per [official docs](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/integrations-guide/cloudflare/) |
| `<ViewTransitions />` renamed to `<ClientRouter />`, event timing changed | Any JS hooking `astro:after-swap` needs retesting | Flag in Phase 2 spec ([GitHub #15191](https://github.com/withastro/astro/issues/15191) via [Southwell Media](https://www.southwellmedia.com/blog/astro-6-whats-coming-2026)) |
| `Astro.glob()` removed in v6 | N/A for new projects | Use `import.meta.glob()` or `getCollection()` |
| Zod 4 upgrade | Standalone `zod` must be replaced with `astro/zod` import | Enforce in lint rule |
| Astro Rust compiler experimental | Don't auto-correct invalid HTML; missing dev-toolbar metadata | Leave on Go compiler (default) until v7 |
| Berkeley Mono v2 licensing change | v2 modularized pricing; web use now an add-on ([Lobsters thread](https://lobste.rs/s/jrutdz/commit_mono)) | Ship with Commit Mono or Ioskeley Mono; swap when license purchased |
| Sandpack requires React | +40 KB gz on playground pages | Island with `client:only="react"` |
| `astro-loader-obsidian` maintenance unknown | May lag Astro major versions | Have hand-rolled import script as backup |
| Cloudflare Workers free-tier 10 ms CPU | `/stats` could exceed on slow upstream | Pre-build snapshot approach (Batch 4.2 option 2) |

---

## 5. "What to Cut First" Under Scope Pressure

Ordered from first-to-cut to last-to-cut:

1. **Phase 7 entirely** — custom cursor, sounds, time-of-day. Zero impact on core value.
2. **Batch 5.5 graph view** — keep the digital garden, drop the visualization. Notes still link.
3. **Batch 3.3 code execution** — replace `<Sandbox>` with static code blocks + "Open in StackBlitz" link.
4. **Batch 2.3 cmd-K palette** — URL filters + a visible search box cover 80 % of the value.
5. **Batch 6.3 webmentions** — leave in `rel="webmention"` link (2 lines) and defer rendering.
6. **Batch 4.2 live /stats** — ship a static "what I've been up to" page with manual updates.

Do **not** cut: Phase 0 (foundations), Batches 1.1–1.3 (card grid), Batch 3.1 (Expressive Code), Batch 6.1 (RSS), Batch 6.2 (sitemap + microformats). These are the cheap, high-leverage essentials.

